# VERDICT 2026-09-04: MEASURED, NOT PROMOTED (v1 chosen by the owner) - structured 65.2, prose 40.4 harness /
# 40.7 by hand, c4 177 (174/180), @1400 60.5, code 47.7, prefill flat, long-context decode 41.9 / 38.2:
# steadiest concurrency, but batch-uniform lets the slowest stream govern k for everyone
# (bench-results/2026-09-04-adaptive-k.md).
# Adaptive k, v4 (2026-09-04 10:30, owner: "v2 e' la piu' bilanciata, facciamo anche v4"): the v2
# thresholds (seed 0.0, band 0.50/0.60) in BATCH-UNIFORM mode: one draft length per step, k=5 only
# when every request with drafts is in the high state, else k=3. Single stream behaves like v2; at
# four streams the verify batch is always uniform, so the FULL decode CUDA graph is used on every
# decode step (per-request mode mixes k across requests and falls back to PIECEWISE on those steps).
# Purpose: explain the bimodal four-stream waves seen in v1/v2/v3 (~38 vs ~54 tok/s per stream with
# 5 drafts per step) and, if they disappear, become the promoted configuration instead of v2.
# Rollback: restart without TP4_ENV.
SPEC_TOKENS=5
SPEC_EXTRA_JSON='"num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size":[[1,1,5],[2,6,3]]'
EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS="--kv-cache-memory=17179869184 --moe-backend triton --scheduler-cls adaptive_k_scheduler.AdaptiveKScheduler"
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV='-v $HOME/tp4/moe-configs/E=288,N=512,device_name=NVIDIA_GB10,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[128,128].json:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/configs/E=288,N=512,device_name=NVIDIA_GB10,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[128,128].json:ro -v $HOME/patches/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:/opt/tp4/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:ro -e PYTHONPATH=/opt/tp4 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_MODE=batch-uniform -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_SEED=0.0 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_DOWN=0.50 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_UP=0.60'
